-- ============================================================
-- Furniture / FF&E Schedule: CommonSpirit+ formulary import
-- ============================================================
-- Source: two vendor-specific CommonSpirit+ furniture formularies
-- (Steelcase and OFS, both dated 2026.10.07), read and transcribed from
-- their vendor-supplied PDFs. The two documents share one Product #
-- numbering scheme (AC/ER/SS/WL/TC) split across manufacturers -- each
-- Product # is a single formulary line item, fulfilled by whichever
-- vendor's sheet lists it. taxonomy_id below preserves that Product #
-- (e.g. AMB-FURN-ER2) for direct traceability back to the source PDF.
--
-- The two source PDFs are image-based (vendor-exported spec sheets, no
-- text layer), so every field here was transcribed by reading the page
-- images rather than extracting real text. Category, manufacturer,
-- location, and general product-line names are high confidence. Exact
-- dimensions/weight capacities/model codes carry normal transcription
-- risk for small print in a scanned table -- spot-check against the
-- source PDFs before issuing these for construction/procurement. Two
-- items (SS8, SS9) had an illegible vendor product line in the source
-- and are flagged in their notes rather than guessed.
--
-- room_furniture linking is intentionally NOT populated here: each item's
-- `location` column captures the formulary's location category (e.g.
-- "Exam/Procedure Room", "Arrival Pause, Subwait"), but several locations
-- (Care Team Zone, GME Admin/Huddle, Infusion Bays) don't map 1:1 onto the
-- 35-room Ambulatory taxonomy in 002_rooms_ambulatory.sql, and guessing
-- room-by-room assignments risks misinforming construction docs. Linking
-- room_furniture rows is a follow-up pass once the design team confirms
-- which rooms actually receive which item.

INSERT INTO furniture (
  taxonomy_id, guideline_scope, name, category, subcategory, manufacturer,
  model, dimensions, weight_capacity, frame_finish, upholstery_spec,
  location, responsibility, notes, product_url
) VALUES
